ACP Agent 7 (#866) — Runs Explorer + Replay + trace/DAG

Replaces the placeholder /admin/control/runs section with a full Runs
Explorer that reuses the canonical `agentsRepo.listAgentRunsRich` hook
(same data path as `AdminAgentRunsPage`).

What ships
----------
- `pages/admin/control/runs/RunsExplorer.tsx` — main UI with:
  * agent picker driven by `?agent=:slug` query param (legacy redirect
    target from `/admin/agents/:slug/runs` already configured by
    Agent 3 in `admin.routes.tsx`).
  * filters: status, period (1h/24h/7d/30d/all), model contains,
    max cost USD, max latency ms, free-text search.
  * compact 24-bucket timeline with success/fail/other segments.
  * runs list with explicit loading / empty / error / refresh states.
  * detail pane: stats grid, sensitive-hold banner, Prompt + Response
    with auto JSON/markdown highlighting, verifier verdict (JSON),
    tool DAG, error block, deep-link to approvals inbox.
- `pages/admin/control/runs/syntax.tsx` — dependency-free regex-based
  JSON + markdown highlighters (escape-then-tokenize, no html
  injection of unsanitized data).
- `pages/admin/control/runs/ToolDag.tsx` — vertical DAG view of
  `tools_used` with parent/child detection, status tone, duration.
- `pages/admin/control/runs/ReplayDialog.tsx` — confirmation dialog
  with editable prompt; dispatches a fresh task through the canonical
  `taskDispatcher` (same path used by ExecutionTaskPanel's Retry),
  with `parentTaskId` linkage and a unique idempotency key. Approval
  is never auto-carried; sensitive types land in `pending_review` and
  the operator is told where to follow up.
- `sections/RunsSection.tsx` rewired to render `RunsExplorer`.

No new dependencies, no edge-function changes, no schema changes. All
mutations go through the existing `taskDispatcher`/`dispatch_execution_task`
RPC — replay is real, not mocked. TS + ESLint clean.

Post-review fixes
-----------------
- ToolDag: orphan tool nodes now chain off the previous node
  (`parentId = prev.id`) so flat tools_used arrays render as a
  sequential DAG instead of a row of disconnected roots.
- ReplayDialog reset effect now keys only on `open` + `runId`
  (excluding the `run` object identity and the mutation handle), so
  the parent's 15s poll cannot wipe operator edits or confirmation
  state mid-flight.

